  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "$\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{4}\u2061x+{cos}^{2}\u2061x{sin}^{2}\u2061x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}\u2061x+{cos}^{2}\u2061x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{4}\u2061x+{cos}^{2}\u2061x{sin}^{2}\u2061x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061x({cos}^{2}\u2061x+{sin}^{2}\u2061x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061x\\cdot 1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
